The vast majority of deaths are due to mistakes.  I am an experienced 
player, and almost every time I die it's because I did something stupid. 
  If mistakes could be eliminated almost all (90-100%, depending on 
class) of conduct-free characters would ascend.

Sometimes it's not easy to see the mistake, though.  If you get killed 
by a monster that is too fast to run from and too tough to kill, there's 
almost always something you could have done to avoid it.  That's a mistake.

Often the mistake is in strategy rather than in tactics.  The biggest 
strategic mistake is probaby descending too slowly or too quickly - 
either can get you killed, sooner or later.  Another mistake is failing 
to identify items that could save your life in otherwise doomed 
situations.  These errors are much harder to recognize and correct.

